# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE IMPORTANT PART — read before editing.
#
# This is a public repo and `data/` will contain recordings of real radio
# traffic involving identifiable people and vessels, some of them in real
# emergencies. Committing that is the single worst mistake available in this
# project, and git history makes it effectively permanent.
#
# Never remove these four rules. If you need to share audio, share it out of
# band — not through the repo. Test fixtures must be synthetic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
audio-test-samples/
*.wav
*.opus
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.aac
*.flac
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Exception: committed synthetic fixtures. These are generated by test code
# with known speech/silence patterns — no real traffic, ever.
!tests/fixtures/*.wav

# Per-machine config. Device names, gain, and calibrated thresholds are
# properties of one rig and do not transfer (docs/decisions.md D11). The
# `.example` files in config/ are the shared templates and ARE committed.
config/config.toml
config/watchwords.toml

# Secrets. They belong in environment variables (VHFWATCH_*), never in a file,
# but ignore the usual suspects in case someone reaches for one anyway.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store
